#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-switch(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:7
msgid "git-switch - Switch branches"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t'git switch' [<options>] [--no-guess] <branch>\n"
"\t'git switch' [<options>] --detach [<start-point>]\n"
"\t'git switch' [<options>] (-c|-C) <new-branch> [<start-point>]\n"
"\t'git switch' [<options>] --orphan <new-branch>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:21
msgid ""
"Switch to a specified branch. The working tree and the index are updated to "
"match the branch. All new commits will be added to the tip of this branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:26
msgid ""
"Optionally a new branch could be created with either `-c`, `-C`, "
"automatically from a remote branch of same name (see `--guess`), or detach "
"the working tree from any branch with `--detach`, along with switching."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:31
msgid ""
"Switching branches does not require a clean index and working tree (i.e. no "
"differences compared to `HEAD`). The operation is aborted however if the "
"operation leads to loss of local changes, unless told otherwise with "
"`--discard-changes` or `--merge`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:33
msgid "THIS COMMAND IS EXPERIMENTAL. THE BEHAVIOR MAY CHANGE."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "<branch>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:38
msgid "Branch to switch to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "<new-branch>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:41
msgid "Name for the new branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "<start-point>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:48
msgid ""
"The starting point for the new branch. Specifying a `<start-point>` allows "
"you to create a branch based on some other point in history than where HEAD "
"currently points. (Or, in the case of `--detach`, allows you to inspect and "
"detach from some other point.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:54
msgid ""
"You can use the `@{-N}` syntax to refer to the N-th last branch/commit "
"switched to using \"git switch\" or \"git checkout\" operation. You may also "
"specify `-` which is synonymous to `@{-1}`.  This is often used to switch "
"quickly between two branches, or to undo a branch switch by mistake."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:58
msgid ""
"As a special case, you may use `A...B` as a shortcut for the merge base of "
"`A` and `B` if there is exactly one merge base. You can leave out at most "
"one of `A` and `B`, in which case it defaults to `HEAD`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-c`\n"
"`--create`\n"
"\tCreate a new branch named `<new-branch>` starting at\n"
"\t`<start-point>` before switching to the branch. This is the\n"
"\ttransactional equivalent of\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git branch <new-branch>\n"
"$ git switch <new-branch>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:74
msgid ""
"that is to say, the branch is not reset/created unless \"git switch\" is "
"successful (e.g., when the branch is in use in another worktree, not just "
"the current branch stays the same, but the branch is not reset to the "
"start-point, either)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:80
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-C`\n"
"`--force-create`\n"
"\tSimilar to `--create` except that if `<new-branch>` already\n"
"\texists, it will be reset to `<start-point>`. This is a\n"
"\tconvenient shortcut for:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:84
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git branch -f <new-branch>\n"
"$ git switch <new-branch>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-d::`\n"
"`--detach::`\n"
"\tSwitch to a commit for inspection and discardable\n"
"\texperiments. See the \"DETACHED HEAD\" section in\n"
"\tlinkgit:git-checkout[1] for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:97
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--guess::`\n"
"`--no-guess::`\n"
"\tIf `<branch>` is not found but there does exist a tracking\n"
"\tbranch in exactly one remote (call it `<remote>`) with a\n"
"\tmatching name, treat as equivalent to\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch -c <branch> --track <remote>/<branch>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:109
msgid ""
"If the branch exists in multiple remotes and one of them is named by the "
"`checkout.defaultRemote` configuration variable, we'll use that one for the "
"purposes of disambiguation, even if the `<branch>` isn't unique across all "
"remotes. Set it to e.g. `checkout.defaultRemote=origin` to always checkout "
"remote branches from there if `<branch>` is ambiguous but exists on the "
"'origin' remote. See also `checkout.defaultRemote` in linkgit:git-config[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:111
msgid "`--guess` is the default behavior. Use `--no-guess` to disable it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:114
msgid ""
"The default behavior can be set via the `checkout.guess` configuration "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:118
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-f::`\n"
"`--force::`\n"
"\tAn alias for `--discard-changes`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--discard-changes::`\n"
"\tProceed even if the index or the working tree differs from\n"
"\t`HEAD`. Both the index and working tree are restored to match\n"
"\tthe switching target. If `--recurse-submodules` is specified,\n"
"\tsubmodule content is also restored to match the switching\n"
"\ttarget. This is used to throw away local changes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:135
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-m::`\n"
"`--merge::`\n"
"\tIf you have local modifications to one or more files that are\n"
"\tdifferent between the current branch and the branch to which\n"
"\tyou are switching, the command refuses to switch branches in\n"
"\torder to preserve your modifications in context.  However,\n"
"\twith this option, a three-way merge between the current\n"
"\tbranch, your working tree contents, and the new branch is\n"
"\tdone, and you will be on the new branch.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:140
msgid ""
"When a merge conflict happens, the index entries for conflicting paths are "
"left unmerged, and you need to resolve the conflicts and mark the resolved "
"paths with `git add` (or `git rm` if the merge should result in deletion of "
"the path)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:146
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--conflict=<style>::`\n"
"\tThe same as `--merge` option above, but changes the way the\n"
"\tconflicting hunks are presented, overriding the\n"
"\t`merge.conflictStyle` configuration variable.  Possible values are\n"
"\t\"merge\" (default), \"diff3\", and \"zdiff3\".\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-q::`\n"
"`--quiet::`\n"
"\tQuiet, suppress feedback messages.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:157
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--progress::`\n"
"`--no-progress::`\n"
"\tProgress status is reported on the standard error stream\n"
"\tby default when it is attached to a terminal, unless `--quiet`\n"
"\tis specified. This flag enables progress reporting even if not\n"
"\tattached to a terminal, regardless of `--quiet`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:163
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-t::`\n"
"`--track`\n"
"\tWhen creating a new branch, set up \"upstream\" configuration.\n"
"\t`-c` is implied. See `--track` in linkgit:git-branch[1] for\n"
"\tdetails.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:173
msgid ""
"If no `-c` option is given, the name of the new branch will be derived from "
"the remote-tracking branch, by looking at the local part of the refspec "
"configured for the corresponding remote, and then stripping the initial part "
"up to the \"*\".  This would tell us to use `hack` as the local branch when "
"branching off of `origin/hack` (or `remotes/origin/hack`, or even "
"`refs/remotes/origin/hack`).  If the given name has no slash, or the above "
"guessing results in an empty name, the guessing is aborted.  You can "
"explicitly give a name with `-c` in such a case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:177
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--no-track::`\n"
"\tDo not set up \"upstream\" configuration, even if the\n"
"\t`branch.autoSetupMerge` configuration variable is true.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:181
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--orphan`\n"
"\tCreate a new unborn branch, named `<new-branch>`. All\n"
"\ttracked files are removed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:187
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--ignore-other-worktrees::`\n"
"\t`git switch` refuses when the wanted ref is already\n"
"\tchecked out by another worktree. This option makes it check\n"
"\tthe ref out anyway. In other words, the ref can be held by\n"
"\tmore than one worktree.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:196
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--recurse-submodules::`\n"
"`--no-recurse-submodules::`\n"
"\tUsing `--recurse-submodules` will update the content of all\n"
"\tactive submodules according to the commit recorded in the\n"
"\tsuperproject. If nothing (or `--no-recurse-submodules`) is\n"
"\tused, submodules working trees will not be updated. Just\n"
"\tlike linkgit:git-submodule[1], this will detach `HEAD` of the\n"
"\tsubmodules.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:198
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:201
msgid "The following command switches to the \"master\" branch:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:204
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch master\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:208
msgid ""
"After working in the wrong branch, switching to the correct branch would be "
"done using:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:211
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch mytopic\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:216
msgid ""
"However, your \"wrong\" branch and correct \"mytopic\" branch may differ in "
"files that you have modified locally, in which case the above switch would "
"fail like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:220
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch mytopic\n"
"error: You have local changes to 'frotz'; not switching branches.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:224
msgid ""
"You can give the `-m` flag to the command, which would try a three-way "
"merge:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:228
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch -m mytopic\n"
"Auto-merging frotz\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:233
msgid ""
"After this three-way merge, the local modifications are _not_ registered in "
"your index file, so `git diff` would show you what changes you made since "
"the tip of the new branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:236
msgid ""
"To switch back to the previous branch before we switched to mytopic "
"(i.e. \"master\" branch):"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:239
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch -\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:243
msgid ""
"You can grow a new branch from any commit. For example, switch to \"HEAD~3\" "
"and create branch \"fixup\":"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:247
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch -c fixup HEAD~3\n"
"Switched to a new branch 'fixup'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:251
msgid "If you want to start a new branch from a remote branch of the same name:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:256
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch new-topic\n"
"Branch 'new-topic' set up to track remote branch 'new-topic' from 'origin'\n"
"Switched to a new branch 'new-topic'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:260
msgid ""
"To check out commit `HEAD~3` for temporary inspection or experiment without "
"creating a new branch:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:264
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git switch --detach HEAD~3\n"
"HEAD is now at 9fc9555312 Merge branch 'cc/shared-index-permbits'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:268
msgid ""
"If it turns out whatever you have done is worth keeping, you can always "
"create a new name for it (without switching away):"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-switch.txt:271
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ git switch -c good-surprises\n"
msgstr ""

